<title>SWEDEN: Swedbank posts 23 pct rise in 9-mo profit.</title>
<headline>Swedbank posts 23 pct rise in 9-mo profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish commercial bank Swedbank results for the nine months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>				     (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			 3,817  vs   3,103</p>
<p> Credit losses			    1,305  vs   1,800</p>
<p> Profit before credit losses	  5,122  vs   4,903</p>
<p> Interest and leasing income	 33,569  vs  36,017</p>
<p> Interest costs			  25,324  vs  27,620</p>
<p> Net of commissions	  CREDIT   1,933  vs   1,432   CREDIT</p>
<p> Net of financial trans    CREDIT     889  vs     753   CREDIT</p>
<p> Other operating income		   656  vs     707</p>
<p> Total income			    11,723  vs  11,289</p>
<p> Staff costs				3,161  vs   3,221</p>
<p> Other admin costs			2,515  vs   2,262</p>
<p> Depreciation				 794  vs     903</p>
<p> Goodwill				     131  vs     nil</p>
<p> Total costs				6,601  vs   6,386</p>
<p> Interest net			     7,621  vs   7,750</p>
<p>NOTE -- Swedbank is known as Sparbanken Sverige AB in Sweden.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll found analysts on average expected Swedbank to post a profit after credit losses of 3.65 billion crowns for the first nine months of the year.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
